  "interpretation": [
    "The original stratified loss reduces active-target error but overpredicts zero elements, making full-vector MSE worse than persistence and zero.",
    "The MSE objective control reduces false positives and beats both persistence and zero in held-out full-vector MSE at H1 and H16; action-conditioned heads beat state-only heads in all three paired fit seeds on this metric.",
    "The action contribution at H1 is small: about 1.35 percent full-vector MSE improvement over state-only and 2.36 percent worsening when action labels are shuffled.",
    "On H1 randomized-action transitions, action heads improve full-vector MSE over state-only in every fit seed, but their active-target MSE remains worse than persistence. Report both metrics.",
    "About 1.5 percent of target elements are active. Positive-baseline results must be interpreted together with active and zero MSE, per-unit support, and the zero predictor.",
    "H16 conditions on the recorded future action prefix. It is a direct behavior-prefix forecast, not a recursively rolled-out or counterfactual world model.",
    "This is one fixed donor and trajectory dataset with three optimizer seeds; it does not establish planning, policy improvement, or downstream reward transfer."
  ],
  "claim_limit": "Offline held-out DG prediction with recorded executed actions; no online policy effect, planning, or counterfactual identification."
}
